{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mNMsmy4HYNNuGRNwMHkmx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: share_docs (Documentation Export)\n     2→\n     3→## Status: ALL PHASES COMPLETE\n     4→\n     5→All 6 steps implemented in iteration 1.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## DONE: Step 1: Add `read_domain_requirements()` to ProgressService\n    10→- Added static method to `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n    11→- Returns Optional[str], handles missing/empty/error cases\n    12→\n    13→## DONE: Step 2: Create ExportService\n    14→- Created `vista/server/services/export_service.py`\n    15→- `get_exportable_features()` scans .vista/features/, returns features with diagrams/requirements\n    16→- `generate_export_html()` collects diagram content + requirements, builds JSON data blob, renders Jinja2 template\n    17→\n    18→## DONE: Step 3: Create Export Routes\n    19→- Created `vista/server/routes/export.py` with GET and POST endpoints\n    20→- Registered router in `vista/server/app.py`\n    21→- GET returns feature tree JSON for modal checklist\n    22→- POST generates and returns HTML file with Content-Disposition attachment header\n    23→\n    24→## DONE: Step 4: Create Export HTML Template\n    25→- Created `vista/server/views/export.html` (standalone, NOT extending _base.html)\n    26→- Dark theme CSS extracted from architecture.html\n    27→- CDN dependencies: Tailwind, Mermaid @11, Marked @15\n    28→- Data embedded as JSON via `|tojson` filter for safe escaping\n    29→- Client-side rendering of Mermaid diagrams and markdown requirements\n    30→- Pan/zoom controls copied from architecture.html\n    31→- Modal overlay for expanded diagram view\n    32→- Feature navigation for multi-feature exports\n    33→- Fixed Jinja2 nested loop indexing using `{% set fi = loop.index0 %}` + `{% set did = fi ~ '-' ~ loop.index0 %}`\n    34→\n    35→## DONE: Step 5: Add Export Modal to Project Page\n    36→- Added \"Export Docs\" button next to \"Remove Project\" in project header\n    37→- Added export modal with tree-style checklist UI\n    38→- Feature checkboxes toggle all child diagrams\n    39→- Individual diagram toggles update parent (checked/indeterminate/unchecked)\n    40→- Select All / Deselect All buttons\n    41→- Download button disabled when nothing selected\n    42→- Export JS uses `escapeHtmlExport()` (renamed to avoid collision with potential existing `escapeHtml`)\n    43→- Uses existing `PROJECT_ID` variable already defined in project.html\n    44→\n    45→## DONE: Step 6: Tests\n    46→- Created `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` with 16 tests\n    47→- 3 tests for ProgressService.read_domain_requirements\n    48→- 5 tests for ExportService.get_exportable_features\n    49→- 5 tests for ExportService.generate_export_html\n    50→- 3 tests for export routes (GET features, POST export, POST 404)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NicdbGFZBazeAx89joE4YR","session_id":"99d2dbda-9327-4d38-9974-87ec95f217c6","uuid":"3c618669-23a9-4957-bdda-a9177c81dbff"}
