{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EouTPk2tTfmzFLJEYNMw4Y","type":"tool_result","content":"   105→\n   106→@router.get(\"/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts\")\n   107→async def list_ralph_artifacts(job_id: str):\n   108→    \"\"\"List artifact files in job directory.\"\"\"\n   109→    _project, _project_root, job_dir = _find_job_context(job_id)\n   110→    # Exclude internal files, show everything else\n   111→    exclude = {\"job.json\", \"output.log\"}\n   112→    artifacts = []\n   113→    for f in sorted(job_dir.iterdir()):\n   114→        if f.is_file() and f.name not in exclude:\n   115→            artifacts.append({\n   116→                \"name\": f.name,\n   117→                \"size\": f.stat().st_size,\n   118→            })\n   119→    # Also include archived job.json files\n   120→    for f in sorted(job_dir.glob(\"job.*.json\")):\n   121→        artifacts.append({\n   122→            \"name\": f.name,\n   123→            \"size\": f.stat().st_size,\n   124→        })\n   125→    return {\"artifacts\": artifacts}\n   126→\n   127→\n   128→@router.get(\"/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename:path}\")\n   129→async def get_ralph_artifact(job_id: str, filename: str):\n   130→    \"\"\"Read contents of a specific artifact file.\"\"\"\n   131→    _project, _project_root, job_dir = _find_job_context(job_id)\n   132→    artifact = job_dir / filename\n   133→    # Security: ensure the resolved path is within the job directory\n   134→    try:\n   135→        artifact.resolve().relative_to(job_dir.resolve())\n   136→    except ValueError:\n   137→        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Invalid artifact path\")\n   138→    if not artifact.exists() or not artifact.is_file():\n   139→        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=f\"Artifact not found: {filename}\")\n   140→    content = artifact.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n   141→    return PlainTextResponse(content)\n   142→\n   143→\n   144→@router.post(\"/jobs/{job_id}/stop\")\n   145→async def stop_ralph_job(job_id: str):\n   146→    \"\"\"Stop a running ralph job.\"\"\"\n   147→    try:\n   148→        project, project_root, _job_dir = _find_job_context(job_id)\n   149→        job = ralph_service.stop_job(project_root, job_id)\n   150→        if not job:\n   151→            raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=f\"Job not found: {job_id}\")\n   152→        job[\"project_name\"] = project.name\n   153→        job[\"project_id\"] = project.id\n   154→        return job\n   155→    except HTTPException:\n   156→        raise\n   157→    except Exception as e:\n   158→        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Failed to stop job: {e}\")\n   159→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NicdbGFZBazeAx89joE4YR","session_id":"99d2dbda-9327-4d38-9974-87ec95f217c6","uuid":"7118902c-d64e-41ba-a4eb-900e90232cf2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Gpn3BG8wXWZ1QcNGL8sbT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Analysis: CDN Dependencies in Export Template\n\n### Overview\nThe `export.html` template currently relies on three CDN-hosted JavaScript libraries for rendering. All templates in the Vista dashboard (`_base.html`, `architecture.html`, `diagram_expand.html`, and `export.html`) share a consistent pattern of using CDN dependencies. There is no existing infrastructure for bundling or vendoring these libraries.\n\n### CDN Dependencies Identified\n\n#### In export.html (lines 7-9)\n1. **Tailwind CSS** - `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`\n   - Purpose: Utility-first CSS framework for styling\n   - Used: Throughout the template for responsive layout and styling\n   \n2. **Mermaid v11** - `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`\n   - Purpose: Diagram rendering engine\n   - Used: Lines 315-329 (initialization), 337-351 (rendering diagrams)\n   \n3. **Marked v15** - `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js`\n   - Purpose: Markdown parser\n   - Used: Line 332 (configuration), 359 (rendering requirements prose)\n\n### CDN Usage Pattern Across Templates\n\n#### _base.html (line 7)\n- Tailwind CSS CDN only\n\n#### architecture.html (lines 6-7)\n- Mermaid v11 CDN\n- Marked v15 CDN\n- Inherits Tailwind CSS from `_base.html`\n\n#### diagram_expand.html (lines 7-9)\n- Identical to export.html: all three CDN dependencies\n\n### Current Static Assets Structure\n\n#### Directory: `vista/server/views/static/`\nContains only custom application code:\n- `app.js` - Ralph Loop Dashboard SSE client and UI interactions\n- `arch-chat.css` - Chat panel styling\n- `arch-chat.js` - Architecture chat functionality (not found in glob, likely unused)\n- `style.css` - Custom dashboard styles\n\n**No vendor/bundled JavaScript libraries exist in the static directory.**\n\n### Key Technical Details\n\n#### Tailwind CSS Integration\n- Uses CDN JIT compiler (`cdn.tailwindcss.com`)\n- Scans HTML at runtime for utility classes\n- No build step required, but creates online dependency\n\n#### Mermaid Usage Pattern (export.html:315-351)\n```javascript\nmermaid.initialize({\n    startOnLoad: false,\n    theme: 'dark',\n    themeVariables: { /* theme config */ }\n});\n\n// Async rendering loop\nfor (const item of EXPORT_DATA.diagrams) {\n    const { svg } = await mermaid.render(renderId, item.content);\n    el.innerHTML = svg;\n}\n```\n\n#### Marked Usage Pattern (export.html:332, 359)\n```javascript\nmarked.setOptions({ breaks: true, gfm: true });\n// Later: rendered via marked.parse(markdown)\nel.innerHTML = marked.parse(markdown);\n```\n\n### Data Flow for Export Template\n\n1. **Template rendering** (Python/Jinja2 at `vista/server/routes/export.py`)\n2. **Embedded data** (line 304-306): Diagrams and requirements as JSON\n3. **Client-side parsing** (line 310-312): Extract embedded `EXPORT_DATA`\n4. **Async diagram rendering** (lines 337-351): Mermaid processes each diagram\n5. **Markdown rendering** (lines 354-361): Marked parses requirements text\n\n### No Existing Bundling Infrastructure\n\n- **No vendor directory** for dashboard static assets\n- **No build tooling** for the dashboard (unlike The Companion which uses Bun)\n- **No package.json** in `vista/server/views/`\n- **Pattern**: All dashboard templates use CDN-only approach for third-party libraries\n\n### Static Asset Serving (FastAPI)\n\nThe dashboard mounts static files at `/static` route (configuration would be in `vista/server/app.py`), serving files from `vista/server/views/static/` directory. This is where bundled assets would need to be placed.\n\n### Summary\n\n**Current state:**\n- 3 CDN dependencies (Tailwind CSS, Mermaid v11, Marked v15)\n- No existing bundled/vendored libraries\n- Consistent CDN-only pattern across all dashboard templates\n- Static directory contains only custom application code\n\n**For offline-first export:**\n- Need to bundle all 3 dependencies\n- Need to embed them inline or serve as data URLs\n- No existing bundling infrastructure to reuse\n- Would be first instance of vendored libraries in the dashboard codebase"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a3fe9cb (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 77219\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 59126</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d2dbda-9327-4d38-9974-87ec95f217c6","uuid":"2886eb05-dd00-4606-898b-667fda265361","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"For the offline-first feature of the Share Docs V2 plan, I need to understand the current CDN dependencies used in the export template. Please:\n\n1. Read vista/server/views/export.html and identify the CDN script URLs\n2. Check if there are any existing vendor/bundled JS files in the project that could be reused\n3. Look at vista/server/views/ for any other templates that use CDN dependencies to understand if there's a pattern for bundling\n4. Check if there's a static assets directory structure (vista/server/views/static/ or similar)\n\nWorking directory: C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization","agentId":"a3fe9cb","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Analysis: CDN Dependencies in Export Template\n\n### Overview\nThe `export.html` template currently relies on three CDN-hosted JavaScript libraries for rendering. All templates in the Vista dashboard (`_base.html`, `architecture.html`, `diagram_expand.html`, and `export.html`) share a consistent pattern of using CDN dependencies. There is no existing infrastructure for bundling or vendoring these libraries.\n\n### CDN Dependencies Identified\n\n#### In export.html (lines 7-9)\n1. **Tailwind CSS** - `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`\n   - Purpose: Utility-first CSS framework for styling\n   - Used: Throughout the template for responsive layout and styling\n   \n2. **Mermaid v11** - `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js`\n   - Purpose: Diagram rendering engine\n   - Used: Lines 315-329 (initialization), 337-351 (rendering diagrams)\n   \n3. **Marked v15** - `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js`\n   - Purpose: Markdown parser\n   - Used: Line 332 (configuration), 359 (rendering requirements prose)\n\n### CDN Usage Pattern Across Templates\n\n#### _base.html (line 7)\n- Tailwind CSS CDN only\n\n#### architecture.html (lines 6-7)\n- Mermaid v11 CDN\n- Marked v15 CDN\n- Inherits Tailwind CSS from `_base.html`\n\n#### diagram_expand.html (lines 7-9)\n- Identical to export.html: all three CDN dependencies\n\n### Current Static Assets Structure\n\n#### Directory: `vista/server/views/static/`\nContains only custom application code:\n- `app.js` - Ralph Loop Dashboard SSE client and UI interactions\n- `arch-chat.css` - Chat panel styling\n- `arch-chat.js` - Architecture chat functionality (not found in glob, likely unused)\n- `style.css` - Custom dashboard styles\n\n**No vendor/bundled JavaScript libraries exist in the static directory.**\n\n### Key Technical Details\n\n#### Tailwind CSS Integration\n- Uses CDN JIT compiler (`cdn.tailwindcss.com`)\n- Scans HTML at runtime for utility classes\n- No build step required, but creates online dependency\n\n#### Mermaid Usage Pattern (export.html:315-351)\n```javascript\nmermaid.initialize({\n    startOnLoad: false,\n    theme: 'dark',\n    themeVariables: { /* theme config */ }\n});\n\n// Async rendering loop\nfor (const item of EXPORT_DATA.diagrams) {\n    const { svg } = await mermaid.render(renderId, item.content);\n    el.innerHTML = svg;\n}\n```\n\n#### Marked Usage Pattern (export.html:332, 359)\n```javascript\nmarked.setOptions({ breaks: true, gfm: true });\n// Later: rendered via marked.parse(markdown)\nel.innerHTML = marked.parse(markdown);\n```\n\n### Data Flow for Export Template\n\n1. **Template rendering** (Python/Jinja2 at `vista/server/routes/export.py`)\n2. **Embedded data** (line 304-306): Diagrams and requirements as JSON\n3. **Client-side parsing** (line 310-312): Extract embedded `EXPORT_DATA`\n4. **Async diagram rendering** (lines 337-351): Mermaid processes each diagram\n5. **Markdown rendering** (lines 354-361): Marked parses requirements text\n\n### No Existing Bundling Infrastructure\n\n- **No vendor directory** for dashboard static assets\n- **No build tooling** for the dashboard (unlike The Companion which uses Bun)\n- **No package.json** in `vista/server/views/`\n- **Pattern**: All dashboard templates use CDN-only approach for third-party libraries\n\n### Static Asset Serving (FastAPI)\n\nThe dashboard mounts static files at `/static` route (configuration would be in `vista/server/app.py`), serving files from `vista/server/views/static/` directory. This is where bundled assets would need to be placed.\n\n### Summary\n\n**Current state:**\n- 3 CDN dependencies (Tailwind CSS, Mermaid v11, Marked v15)\n- No existing bundled/vendored libraries\n- Consistent CDN-only pattern across all dashboard templates\n- Static directory contains only custom application code\n\n**For offline-first export:**\n- Need to bundle all 3 dependencies\n- Need to embed them inline or serve as data URLs\n- No existing bundling infrastructure to reuse\n- Would be first instance of vendored libraries in the dashboard codebase"}],"totalDurationMs":59126,"totalTokens":77219,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21688,"cache_read_input_tokens":54408,"output_tokens":1117,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21688,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X5SUDSo81xnyxdSE9f57dW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive analysis of the config and settings patterns in this codebase.\n\n## Analysis: Configuration and Settings Patterns in Vista\n\n### Overview\nVista uses a layered configuration system with JSON-based persistence for both global settings and per-entity data. Settings live in `~/.vista/settings.json`, while operational data (projects, sessions, ralph jobs) is stored in `~/.vista/data/` and project-local `.vista/` directories. The codebase follows a dataclass + JSON file persistence pattern without a database.\n\n### Entry Points\n\n#### Global Configuration\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\config.py` - Central configuration module defining all paths and settings access\n\n#### Service Layer\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py` - Project registry CRUD\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py` - Chat session persistence\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py` - Ralph job lifecycle\n\n#### Data Models\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\project.py` - Project model\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py` - Chat session and message models\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\loop_state.py` - Loop state model\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\sandbox.py` - Sandbox configuration models\n\n---\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n#### 1. Directory Structure (`config.py:8-17`)\n\n```python\nPLUGIN_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent  # vista/\nSERVER_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent  # vista/server/\nPORTABLE_DIR = PLUGIN_ROOT / \"portable\"\nTEMPLATES_DIR = PORTABLE_DIR / \"templates\"\nDATA_DIR = Path.home() / \".vista\" / \"data\"\nPROJECTS_FILE = DATA_DIR / \"projects.json\"\n_LEGACY_DATA_DIR = SERVER_DIR / \"data\"  # pre-1.3.12: inside plugin install dir\nVIEWS_DIR = SERVER_DIR / \"views\"\nSTATIC_DIR = VIEWS_DIR / \"static\"\n```\n\n**Data Storage Locations:**\n- **Global settings**: `~/.vista/settings.json` (persistent user settings)\n- **Legacy settings**: `vista/settings.json` (migrated on first load at `config.py:129-149`)\n- **Global data**: `~/.vista/data/` (projects.json, sessions/)\n- **Project data**: `{project_path}/.vista/` (features/, ralph/)\n\n#### 2. Settings File Resolution (`config.py:23-36`)\n\nThe settings file path is resolved with environment variable override support:\n\n```python\ndef _resolve_settings_file() -> Path:\n    override = os.environ.get(\"VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE\", \"\").strip()\n    if override:\n        return Path(override).expanduser().resolve()\n    return Path.home() / \".vista\" / \"settings.json\"\n```\n\n**Settings Sections with Defaults:**\n- `server` (`config.py:38-43`) - Dashboard host/port, auto-start flags\n- `ralph` (`config.py:45-56`) - Provider/model defaults, summarizer config\n- `sandbox` (`config.py:58-70`) - Docker sandbox configuration\n- `tools.teams` (`config.py:72-80`) - Claude/OpenCode binaries and ports\n- `diagrams` (`config.py:91-93`) - PlantUML server URL\n- `chat` (`config.py:104-107`) - Companion and OpenCode port settings\n\n#### 3. Settings Loading and Merging (`config.py:118-159`)\n\nSettings are loaded with a migration step and deep-merge with defaults:\n\n```python\ndef load_settings() -> dict:\n    _migrate_legacy_settings_if_needed()\n    if SETTINGS_FILE.exists():\n        try:\n            return json.loads(SETTINGS_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n            pass\n    return {}\n```\n\nThe `_merge_dicts()` function at `config.py:152-159` recursively merges user settings over defaults, preserving nested structures.\n\n#### 4. Settings Persistence (`config.py:189-197`)\n\nSettings are saved atomically using a temporary file pattern:\n\n```python\ndef save_ralph_settings(ralph_config: dict) -> None:\n    _migrate_legacy_settings_if_needed()\n    settings = load_settings()\n    settings[\"ralph\"] = ralph_config\n    SETTINGS_FILE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp_file = SETTINGS_FILE.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\")\n    tmp_file.write_text(json.dumps(settings, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    tmp_file.replace(SETTINGS_FILE)\n```\n\nThis pattern (write to `.tmp`, then replace) is used for atomic writes at:\n- `config.py:195-197` - Ralph settings save\n- `config.py:218-222` - Sandbox settings save (delegates to `save_ralph_settings`)\n\n---\n\n### Data Persistence Patterns\n\n#### Pattern 1: Global Registry File (`ProjectService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: Single JSON file at `~/.vista/data/projects.json` containing an array of project dictionaries.\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_ensure_file()` (`project_service.py:62-67`) - Creates `DATA_DIR` and empty `[]` file if missing\n- `_load()` (`project_service.py:70-72`) - Reads and parses the JSON array\n- `_save()` (`project_service.py:75-77`) - Writes the array back with 2-space indent\n- `get_all()` (`project_service.py:80-82`) - Returns list of `Project` dataclass instances\n- `register()` (`project_service.py:93-112`) - Appends new project and saves\n\n**Migration**: Legacy data from `vista/server/data/projects.json` is migrated on first access at `project_service.py:43-59`.\n\n#### Pattern 2: Per-Entity JSON Files (`ChatSessionService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: One JSON file per session at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`.\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_session_dir()` (`chat_session_service.py:21-22`) - Computes `SESSIONS_DIR / project_id`\n- `_session_file()` (`chat_session_service.py:25-26`) - Computes full file path\n- `_save()` (`chat_session_service.py:114-118`) - Creates parent dir, writes JSON with 2-space indent\n- `_load()` (`chat_session_service.py:121-123`) - Reads JSON and constructs `ChatSession` from dict\n- `list_sessions()` (`chat_session_service.py:49-65`) - Scans directory, loads all `.json` files, returns summary dicts\n- `get()` (`chat_session_service.py:68-72`) - Loads single session by ID\n- `delete()` (`chat_session_service.py:75-80`) - Unlinks the file\n\n**Sorting**: Sessions are sorted by `st_mtime` (modification time) in descending order at `chat_session_service.py:57`.\n\n#### Pattern 3: Job Directories with Metadata (`RalphService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: Directory per job at `{project_root}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` containing:\n- `job.json` - Job metadata (status, timestamps, PIDs)\n- `output.log` - Subprocess stdout capture\n- `task.md` - User task description\n- `PROMPT_{mode}.md` - Generated prompt file\n- `loop.sh` / `loop.ps1` - Generated loop script\n- `progress.txt` - Inter-loop agent context\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - Generated plan artifact\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_job_dir()` (`ralph_service.py:548-555`) - Computes safe directory name from slug + job_id\n- `_save_job_json()` (`ralph_service.py:587-589`) - Writes job.json with 2-space indent\n- `_load_job_json()` (`ralph_service.py:578-585`) - Loads job.json, returns dict or None\n- `list_jobs()` (`ralph_service.py:534-546`) - Scans ralph directory, loads all job.json files, sorts by `created_at`\n- `get_job_status()` (`ralph_service.py:324-399`) - Loads job, checks process status, parses output.log for progress\n\n**Directory Naming**: Jobs for the same slug get unique suffixes like `feature-name-{uuid}` at `ralph_service.py:555`.\n\n**Runtime Artifacts Cleanup**: Transient files are deleted before job start at `ralph_service.py:709-723`.\n\n---\n\n### Pydantic Model Patterns\n\n#### Model 1: Dataclass with `to_dict()` / `from_dict()` (`Project`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\project.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str = field(default_factory=lambda: str(uuid.uuid4())[:8])\n    name: str = \"\"\n    path: str = \"\"\n    created_at: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n    last_accessed: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return asdict(self)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"Project\":\n        return cls(**{k: v for k, v in data.items() if k in cls.__dataclass_fields__})\n```\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n1. Service layer calls `from_dict()` when loading from JSON\n2. Service layer calls `to_dict()` before saving to JSON\n3. IDs are 8-character UUID prefixes (e.g., `a3f9b2c1`)\n\n#### Model 2: Dataclass with Summary Variant (`ChatSession`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ChatSession:\n    id: str\n    project_id: str\n    feature_name: str\n    name: str\n    provider: str\n    model: str\n    messages: list[ChatMessage] = field(default_factory=list)\n    created_at: str = \"\"\n    updated_at: str = \"\"\n    team_name: Optional[str] = None\n    backend_session_id: Optional[str] = None\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        # Returns full session including all messages\n        \n    def to_summary_dict(self) -> dict:\n        # Returns session metadata without message bodies (for listing)\n```\n\n**Summary Pattern**: `to_summary_dict()` at `chat_session.py:67-81` returns lightweight metadata with `message_count` instead of full message list, used by listing endpoints.\n\n#### Model 3: Nested Dataclass (`ChatMessage`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py:9-26`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ChatMessage:\n    role: str  # \"user\" | \"assistant\"\n    content: str\n    timestamp: str = \"\"\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if not self.timestamp:\n            self.timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n```\n\nMessages are nested within `ChatSession.messages` and serialized/deserialized by list comprehension at `chat_session.py:60` and `chat_session.py:85`.\n\n#### Model 4: Runtime State (Non-Persisted) (`LoopInstance`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\loop_state.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass LoopInstance:\n    project_id: str = \"\"\n    feature_name: str = \"\"\n    mode: str = \"\"\n    model: str = \"\"\n    provider: str = \"\"\n    status: str = \"idle\"\n    pid: Optional[int] = None\n    iteration: int = 0\n    max_iterations: int = 0\n    output_lines: deque = field(default_factory=lambda: deque(maxlen=2000))\n    recent_actions: deque = field(default_factory=lambda: deque(maxlen=20))\n    # ...\n```\n\nThis model is **not persisted** to disk. It's held in memory by `LoopService._loops` dict at `loop_service.py:234` and updated as subprocess output is parsed.\n\n---\n\n### Route Patterns\n\n#### Pattern 1: RESTful CRUD with Pydantic Request Models\n\n**Example**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat_sessions.py`\n\n**Request Models** (`chat_sessions.py:66-85`):\n```python\nclass CreateSessionRequest(BaseModel):\n    feature_name: str\n    provider: str\n    model: str\n    name: str = \"\"\n\nclass SendMessageRequest(BaseModel):\n    message: str\n    context: Optional[str] = None\n    provider: Optional[str] = None\n    model: Optional[str] = None\n```\n\n**CRUD Endpoints**:\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` (`chat_sessions.py:101-115`) - Create\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` (`chat_sessions.py:93-98`) - List\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:118-123`) - Get\n- `DELETE /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:126-134`) - Delete\n- `PATCH /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:137-142`) - Update (rename)\n\n#### Pattern 2: Cross-Project Job Lookup\n\n**Example**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py:16-38`\n\n```python\ndef _find_job_context(job_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Find a ralph job across all registered projects.\"\"\"\n    for project in ProjectService.get_all():\n        project_root = Path(project.path)\n        ralph_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\"\n        if not ralph_dir.exists():\n            continue\n        for slug_dir in ralph_dir.iterdir():\n            if not slug_dir.is_dir():\n                continue\n            job_file = slug_dir / \"job.json\"\n            if not job_file.exists():\n                continue\n            try:\n                data = json.loads(job_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                if data.get(\"job_id\") == job_id:\n                    return project, project_root, slug_dir\n            except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n                continue\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=f\"Job not found: {job_id}\")\n```\n\nThis pattern scans all registered projects to find a job by ID, used by endpoints at `ralph.py:56`, `ralph.py:68`, etc.\n\n---\n\n### Key Configuration Access Functions\n\n#### 1. Ralph Settings (`config.py:162-187`)\n\n- `get_ralph_settings()` - Returns merged ralph config (defaults + user overrides)\n- `get_ralph_defaults()` - Returns provider/model/iterations for ralph_start\n- `get_summarizer_config()` - Returns summarizer provider/model\n- `save_ralph_settings(dict)` - Persists ralph section to settings.json\n\n#### 2. Sandbox Settings (`config.py:200-223`)\n\n- `get_sandbox_settings()` - Returns merged sandbox config\n- `is_sandbox_enabled()` - Boolean check for sandbox mode\n- `get_sandbox_credential_mounts()` - Returns credential_mounts section\n- `save_sandbox_settings(dict)` - Persists sandbox under ralph section\n- `validate_sandbox_settings(dict)` - Returns list of validation errors\n\n#### 3. Server Settings (`config.py:263-300`)\n\n- `get_server_settings()` - Returns merged server config with env var overrides\n- Environment variable overrides: `RALPH_SERVER_HOST`, `RALPH_SERVER_PORT`, `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_START`, `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_OPEN`\n- Special pytest handling to disable auto-open during tests at `config.py:292-298`\n\n#### 4. Diagram Settings (`config.py:96-101`)\n\n- `get_diagram_settings()` - Returns merged diagram config (PlantUML server URL)\n\n#### 5. Chat Settings (`config.py:110-115`)\n\n- `get_chat_settings()` - Returns chat backend ports (Companion, OpenCode)\n\n---\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n#### Project Registration Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/projects` with path\n2. `projects.py` route calls `ProjectService.register(path)`\n3. `project_service.py:93-112` validates path, creates `Project` dataclass instance\n4. `_save()` writes entire projects array to `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n5. Response returns `project.to_dict()`\n\n#### Chat Session Creation Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` with feature_name/provider/model\n2. `chat_sessions.py:101-115` validates project exists\n3. `ChatSessionService.create()` at `chat_session_service.py:29-46` creates `ChatSession` with generated ID\n4. `_save()` writes JSON to `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`\n5. Response returns `session.to_dict()`\n\n#### Ralph Job Creation Flow\n1. User calls `ralph_start` MCP tool with slug/mode/task\n2. `RalphService.create_job()` at `ralph_service.py:43-72` branches on sandbox flag\n3. `_create_native_job()` at `ralph_service.py:74-176` creates job directory under `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/`\n4. Writes `job.json`, `task.md`, `PROMPT_{mode}.md`, `loop.sh`/`loop.ps1`\n5. Spawns subprocess with stdout redirected to `output.log`\n6. Job status polled via `get_job_status()` which parses `output.log` for progress\n\n#### Settings Save Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/ralph/settings` with config\n2. Route validates config with `validate_sandbox_settings()`\n3. Calls `save_ralph_settings()` or `save_sandbox_settings()`\n4. `config.py:189-197` loads current settings, merges new section, writes atomically via `.tmp` file\n5. `tmp_file.replace(SETTINGS_FILE)` performs atomic rename\n\n---\n\n### File Paths Reference\n\n**Global Settings & Data:**\n- `~/.vista/settings.json` - User settings (persistent)\n- `~/.vista/data/projects.json` - Project registry\n- `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` - Chat sessions\n\n**Project-Local Data:**\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/` - Feature specs, plans, diagrams\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/arch/_arch.json` - Diagram manifest\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/specs/*.md` - Spec files\n- `{project}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/job.json` - Ralph job metadata\n- `{project}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/output.log` - Job output\n\n**Templates:**\n- `vista/portable/templates/PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md` - Plan mode prompt template\n- `vista/portable/templates/PROMPT_build_adhoc.md` - Build mode prompt template"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a837e79 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 52010\ntool_uses: 15\nduration_ms: 119654</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d2dbda-9327-4d38-9974-87ec95f217c6","uuid":"c65fa17d-4960-4ba2-9331-a91418d7afc4","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the config and settings patterns in this project for planning an \"export history\" feature. Please:\n\n1. Read vista/server/config.py to understand the config patterns (DATA_DIR, VIEWS_DIR, etc.)\n2. Check if there's a settings service or settings model at vista/server/services/ or vista/server/models/\n3. Look at how project data is persisted (ProjectService, any JSON storage patterns)\n4. Check vista/server/models/ for existing Pydantic models to understand the model patterns used\n\nWorking directory: C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization","agentId":"a837e79","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough context. Let me create a comprehensive analysis of the config and settings patterns in this codebase.\n\n## Analysis: Configuration and Settings Patterns in Vista\n\n### Overview\nVista uses a layered configuration system with JSON-based persistence for both global settings and per-entity data. Settings live in `~/.vista/settings.json`, while operational data (projects, sessions, ralph jobs) is stored in `~/.vista/data/` and project-local `.vista/` directories. The codebase follows a dataclass + JSON file persistence pattern without a database.\n\n### Entry Points\n\n#### Global Configuration\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\config.py` - Central configuration module defining all paths and settings access\n\n#### Service Layer\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py` - Project registry CRUD\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py` - Chat session persistence\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py` - Ralph job lifecycle\n\n#### Data Models\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\project.py` - Project model\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py` - Chat session and message models\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\loop_state.py` - Loop state model\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\sandbox.py` - Sandbox configuration models\n\n---\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n#### 1. Directory Structure (`config.py:8-17`)\n\n```python\nPLUGIN_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent  # vista/\nSERVER_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent  # vista/server/\nPORTABLE_DIR = PLUGIN_ROOT / \"portable\"\nTEMPLATES_DIR = PORTABLE_DIR / \"templates\"\nDATA_DIR = Path.home() / \".vista\" / \"data\"\nPROJECTS_FILE = DATA_DIR / \"projects.json\"\n_LEGACY_DATA_DIR = SERVER_DIR / \"data\"  # pre-1.3.12: inside plugin install dir\nVIEWS_DIR = SERVER_DIR / \"views\"\nSTATIC_DIR = VIEWS_DIR / \"static\"\n```\n\n**Data Storage Locations:**\n- **Global settings**: `~/.vista/settings.json` (persistent user settings)\n- **Legacy settings**: `vista/settings.json` (migrated on first load at `config.py:129-149`)\n- **Global data**: `~/.vista/data/` (projects.json, sessions/)\n- **Project data**: `{project_path}/.vista/` (features/, ralph/)\n\n#### 2. Settings File Resolution (`config.py:23-36`)\n\nThe settings file path is resolved with environment variable override support:\n\n```python\ndef _resolve_settings_file() -> Path:\n    override = os.environ.get(\"VISTA_SETTINGS_FILE\", \"\").strip()\n    if override:\n        return Path(override).expanduser().resolve()\n    return Path.home() / \".vista\" / \"settings.json\"\n```\n\n**Settings Sections with Defaults:**\n- `server` (`config.py:38-43`) - Dashboard host/port, auto-start flags\n- `ralph` (`config.py:45-56`) - Provider/model defaults, summarizer config\n- `sandbox` (`config.py:58-70`) - Docker sandbox configuration\n- `tools.teams` (`config.py:72-80`) - Claude/OpenCode binaries and ports\n- `diagrams` (`config.py:91-93`) - PlantUML server URL\n- `chat` (`config.py:104-107`) - Companion and OpenCode port settings\n\n#### 3. Settings Loading and Merging (`config.py:118-159`)\n\nSettings are loaded with a migration step and deep-merge with defaults:\n\n```python\ndef load_settings() -> dict:\n    _migrate_legacy_settings_if_needed()\n    if SETTINGS_FILE.exists():\n        try:\n            return json.loads(SETTINGS_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n            pass\n    return {}\n```\n\nThe `_merge_dicts()` function at `config.py:152-159` recursively merges user settings over defaults, preserving nested structures.\n\n#### 4. Settings Persistence (`config.py:189-197`)\n\nSettings are saved atomically using a temporary file pattern:\n\n```python\ndef save_ralph_settings(ralph_config: dict) -> None:\n    _migrate_legacy_settings_if_needed()\n    settings = load_settings()\n    settings[\"ralph\"] = ralph_config\n    SETTINGS_FILE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp_file = SETTINGS_FILE.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\")\n    tmp_file.write_text(json.dumps(settings, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    tmp_file.replace(SETTINGS_FILE)\n```\n\nThis pattern (write to `.tmp`, then replace) is used for atomic writes at:\n- `config.py:195-197` - Ralph settings save\n- `config.py:218-222` - Sandbox settings save (delegates to `save_ralph_settings`)\n\n---\n\n### Data Persistence Patterns\n\n#### Pattern 1: Global Registry File (`ProjectService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: Single JSON file at `~/.vista/data/projects.json` containing an array of project dictionaries.\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_ensure_file()` (`project_service.py:62-67`) - Creates `DATA_DIR` and empty `[]` file if missing\n- `_load()` (`project_service.py:70-72`) - Reads and parses the JSON array\n- `_save()` (`project_service.py:75-77`) - Writes the array back with 2-space indent\n- `get_all()` (`project_service.py:80-82`) - Returns list of `Project` dataclass instances\n- `register()` (`project_service.py:93-112`) - Appends new project and saves\n\n**Migration**: Legacy data from `vista/server/data/projects.json` is migrated on first access at `project_service.py:43-59`.\n\n#### Pattern 2: Per-Entity JSON Files (`ChatSessionService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\chat_session_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: One JSON file per session at `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`.\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_session_dir()` (`chat_session_service.py:21-22`) - Computes `SESSIONS_DIR / project_id`\n- `_session_file()` (`chat_session_service.py:25-26`) - Computes full file path\n- `_save()` (`chat_session_service.py:114-118`) - Creates parent dir, writes JSON with 2-space indent\n- `_load()` (`chat_session_service.py:121-123`) - Reads JSON and constructs `ChatSession` from dict\n- `list_sessions()` (`chat_session_service.py:49-65`) - Scans directory, loads all `.json` files, returns summary dicts\n- `get()` (`chat_session_service.py:68-72`) - Loads single session by ID\n- `delete()` (`chat_session_service.py:75-80`) - Unlinks the file\n\n**Sorting**: Sessions are sorted by `st_mtime` (modification time) in descending order at `chat_session_service.py:57`.\n\n#### Pattern 3: Job Directories with Metadata (`RalphService`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py`\n\n**Storage**: Directory per job at `{project_root}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/` containing:\n- `job.json` - Job metadata (status, timestamps, PIDs)\n- `output.log` - Subprocess stdout capture\n- `task.md` - User task description\n- `PROMPT_{mode}.md` - Generated prompt file\n- `loop.sh` / `loop.ps1` - Generated loop script\n- `progress.txt` - Inter-loop agent context\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - Generated plan artifact\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_job_dir()` (`ralph_service.py:548-555`) - Computes safe directory name from slug + job_id\n- `_save_job_json()` (`ralph_service.py:587-589`) - Writes job.json with 2-space indent\n- `_load_job_json()` (`ralph_service.py:578-585`) - Loads job.json, returns dict or None\n- `list_jobs()` (`ralph_service.py:534-546`) - Scans ralph directory, loads all job.json files, sorts by `created_at`\n- `get_job_status()` (`ralph_service.py:324-399`) - Loads job, checks process status, parses output.log for progress\n\n**Directory Naming**: Jobs for the same slug get unique suffixes like `feature-name-{uuid}` at `ralph_service.py:555`.\n\n**Runtime Artifacts Cleanup**: Transient files are deleted before job start at `ralph_service.py:709-723`.\n\n---\n\n### Pydantic Model Patterns\n\n#### Model 1: Dataclass with `to_dict()` / `from_dict()` (`Project`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\project.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Project:\n    id: str = field(default_factory=lambda: str(uuid.uuid4())[:8])\n    name: str = \"\"\n    path: str = \"\"\n    created_at: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n    last_accessed: str = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now().isoformat())\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return asdict(self)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"Project\":\n        return cls(**{k: v for k, v in data.items() if k in cls.__dataclass_fields__})\n```\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n1. Service layer calls `from_dict()` when loading from JSON\n2. Service layer calls `to_dict()` before saving to JSON\n3. IDs are 8-character UUID prefixes (e.g., `a3f9b2c1`)\n\n#### Model 2: Dataclass with Summary Variant (`ChatSession`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ChatSession:\n    id: str\n    project_id: str\n    feature_name: str\n    name: str\n    provider: str\n    model: str\n    messages: list[ChatMessage] = field(default_factory=list)\n    created_at: str = \"\"\n    updated_at: str = \"\"\n    team_name: Optional[str] = None\n    backend_session_id: Optional[str] = None\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        # Returns full session including all messages\n        \n    def to_summary_dict(self) -> dict:\n        # Returns session metadata without message bodies (for listing)\n```\n\n**Summary Pattern**: `to_summary_dict()` at `chat_session.py:67-81` returns lightweight metadata with `message_count` instead of full message list, used by listing endpoints.\n\n#### Model 3: Nested Dataclass (`ChatMessage`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\chat_session.py:9-26`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ChatMessage:\n    role: str  # \"user\" | \"assistant\"\n    content: str\n    timestamp: str = \"\"\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if not self.timestamp:\n            self.timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n```\n\nMessages are nested within `ChatSession.messages` and serialized/deserialized by list comprehension at `chat_session.py:60` and `chat_session.py:85`.\n\n#### Model 4: Runtime State (Non-Persisted) (`LoopInstance`)\n\n**Location**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\models\\loop_state.py`\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass LoopInstance:\n    project_id: str = \"\"\n    feature_name: str = \"\"\n    mode: str = \"\"\n    model: str = \"\"\n    provider: str = \"\"\n    status: str = \"idle\"\n    pid: Optional[int] = None\n    iteration: int = 0\n    max_iterations: int = 0\n    output_lines: deque = field(default_factory=lambda: deque(maxlen=2000))\n    recent_actions: deque = field(default_factory=lambda: deque(maxlen=20))\n    # ...\n```\n\nThis model is **not persisted** to disk. It's held in memory by `LoopService._loops` dict at `loop_service.py:234` and updated as subprocess output is parsed.\n\n---\n\n### Route Patterns\n\n#### Pattern 1: RESTful CRUD with Pydantic Request Models\n\n**Example**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\chat_sessions.py`\n\n**Request Models** (`chat_sessions.py:66-85`):\n```python\nclass CreateSessionRequest(BaseModel):\n    feature_name: str\n    provider: str\n    model: str\n    name: str = \"\"\n\nclass SendMessageRequest(BaseModel):\n    message: str\n    context: Optional[str] = None\n    provider: Optional[str] = None\n    model: Optional[str] = None\n```\n\n**CRUD Endpoints**:\n- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` (`chat_sessions.py:101-115`) - Create\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` (`chat_sessions.py:93-98`) - List\n- `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:118-123`) - Get\n- `DELETE /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:126-134`) - Delete\n- `PATCH /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions/{session_id}` (`chat_sessions.py:137-142`) - Update (rename)\n\n#### Pattern 2: Cross-Project Job Lookup\n\n**Example**: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py:16-38`\n\n```python\ndef _find_job_context(job_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Find a ralph job across all registered projects.\"\"\"\n    for project in ProjectService.get_all():\n        project_root = Path(project.path)\n        ralph_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\"\n        if not ralph_dir.exists():\n            continue\n        for slug_dir in ralph_dir.iterdir():\n            if not slug_dir.is_dir():\n                continue\n            job_file = slug_dir / \"job.json\"\n            if not job_file.exists():\n                continue\n            try:\n                data = json.loads(job_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                if data.get(\"job_id\") == job_id:\n                    return project, project_root, slug_dir\n            except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n                continue\n    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=f\"Job not found: {job_id}\")\n```\n\nThis pattern scans all registered projects to find a job by ID, used by endpoints at `ralph.py:56`, `ralph.py:68`, etc.\n\n---\n\n### Key Configuration Access Functions\n\n#### 1. Ralph Settings (`config.py:162-187`)\n\n- `get_ralph_settings()` - Returns merged ralph config (defaults + user overrides)\n- `get_ralph_defaults()` - Returns provider/model/iterations for ralph_start\n- `get_summarizer_config()` - Returns summarizer provider/model\n- `save_ralph_settings(dict)` - Persists ralph section to settings.json\n\n#### 2. Sandbox Settings (`config.py:200-223`)\n\n- `get_sandbox_settings()` - Returns merged sandbox config\n- `is_sandbox_enabled()` - Boolean check for sandbox mode\n- `get_sandbox_credential_mounts()` - Returns credential_mounts section\n- `save_sandbox_settings(dict)` - Persists sandbox under ralph section\n- `validate_sandbox_settings(dict)` - Returns list of validation errors\n\n#### 3. Server Settings (`config.py:263-300`)\n\n- `get_server_settings()` - Returns merged server config with env var overrides\n- Environment variable overrides: `RALPH_SERVER_HOST`, `RALPH_SERVER_PORT`, `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_START`, `RALPH_SERVER_AUTO_OPEN`\n- Special pytest handling to disable auto-open during tests at `config.py:292-298`\n\n#### 4. Diagram Settings (`config.py:96-101`)\n\n- `get_diagram_settings()` - Returns merged diagram config (PlantUML server URL)\n\n#### 5. Chat Settings (`config.py:110-115`)\n\n- `get_chat_settings()` - Returns chat backend ports (Companion, OpenCode)\n\n---\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n#### Project Registration Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/projects` with path\n2. `projects.py` route calls `ProjectService.register(path)`\n3. `project_service.py:93-112` validates path, creates `Project` dataclass instance\n4. `_save()` writes entire projects array to `~/.vista/data/projects.json`\n5. Response returns `project.to_dict()`\n\n#### Chat Session Creation Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/chat/sessions` with feature_name/provider/model\n2. `chat_sessions.py:101-115` validates project exists\n3. `ChatSessionService.create()` at `chat_session_service.py:29-46` creates `ChatSession` with generated ID\n4. `_save()` writes JSON to `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json`\n5. Response returns `session.to_dict()`\n\n#### Ralph Job Creation Flow\n1. User calls `ralph_start` MCP tool with slug/mode/task\n2. `RalphService.create_job()` at `ralph_service.py:43-72` branches on sandbox flag\n3. `_create_native_job()` at `ralph_service.py:74-176` creates job directory under `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/`\n4. Writes `job.json`, `task.md`, `PROMPT_{mode}.md`, `loop.sh`/`loop.ps1`\n5. Spawns subprocess with stdout redirected to `output.log`\n6. Job status polled via `get_job_status()` which parses `output.log` for progress\n\n#### Settings Save Flow\n1. User calls `POST /api/ralph/settings` with config\n2. Route validates config with `validate_sandbox_settings()`\n3. Calls `save_ralph_settings()` or `save_sandbox_settings()`\n4. `config.py:189-197` loads current settings, merges new section, writes atomically via `.tmp` file\n5. `tmp_file.replace(SETTINGS_FILE)` performs atomic rename\n\n---\n\n### File Paths Reference\n\n**Global Settings & Data:**\n- `~/.vista/settings.json` - User settings (persistent)\n- `~/.vista/data/projects.json` - Project registry\n- `~/.vista/data/sessions/{project_id}/{session_id}.json` - Chat sessions\n\n**Project-Local Data:**\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/` - Feature specs, plans, diagrams\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/arch/_arch.json` - Diagram manifest\n- `{project}/.vista/features/{feature}/specs/*.md` - Spec files\n- `{project}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/job.json` - Ralph job metadata\n- `{project}/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}/output.log` - Job output\n\n**Templates:**\n- `vista/portable/templates/PROMPT_plan_adhoc.md` - Plan mode prompt template\n- `vista/portable/templates/PROMPT_build_adhoc.md` - Build mode prompt template"}],"totalDurationMs":119654,"totalTokens":52010,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7250,"cache_read_input_tokens":39452,"output_tokens":5301,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NicdbGFZBazeAx89joE4YR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a complete understanding of the Ralph job structure. Let me create the comprehensive analysis.\n\n## Analysis: Ralph Job Structure and Data Access\n\n### Overview\nRalph jobs are autonomous development loops that execute planning or build tasks. Each job creates a directory under `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` containing job metadata (job.json), execution logs (output.log, progress.txt), task description (task.md), prompts (PROMPT_{mode}.md), and implementation plans (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md). The system provides APIs to list, monitor, and retrieve artifacts from these jobs.\n\n### Entry Points\n\n**Job Creation:**\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:43-72` - `RalphService.create_job()` method\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:74-176` - `_create_native_job()` for local subprocess execution\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:178-322` - `_create_sandboxed_job()` for Docker container execution\n\n**Job Access APIs:**\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:41-53` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs` - List all jobs across projects\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:56-65` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` - Get single job with status\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:68-92` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` - Get parsed activity\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:95-103` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` - Get raw output log\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:106-125` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` - List artifact files\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:128-141` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename:path}` - Read artifact content\n\n**Dashboard Views:**\n- `vista/server/views/ralph_job_detail.html:1-247` - Individual job detail page\n- `vista/server/views/ralph_jobs.html` - Job list page\n- `vista/server/views/project.html:97-194` - Ralph Loops tab in project page\n\n### Core Ralph Job Directory Structure\n\n#### Standard Files (Created by RalphService)\n\n**job.json** (`ralph_service.py:158-175` for native, `303-320` for sandboxed)\n```json\n{\n  \"job_id\": \"uuid-string\",\n  \"slug\": \"feature-name-mode\",\n  \"mode\": \"plan|build\",\n  \"status\": \"running|completed|failed|stopped\",\n  \"provider\": \"claude|opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"opus|sonnet\",\n  \"iterations\": 3,\n  \"current_iteration\": 0,\n  \"pid\": 12345,              // null for sandboxed jobs\n  \"sandbox\": false,\n  \"container_id\": null,      // Docker container ID for sandboxed jobs\n  \"created_at\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"started_at\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"completed_at\": \"ISO-8601|null\",\n  \"error\": \"error message|null\",\n  \"progress_tail\": [\"line1\", \"line2\", ...]  // Added during status queries\n}\n```\n\n**task.md** (`ralph_service.py:98-99`)\n- Created in feature directory for plan mode, job directory for build mode\n- Contains the task description passed to `create_job()`\n\n**PROMPT_{mode}.md** (`ralph_service.py:101-111`)\n- Generated from template at `vista/templates/PROMPT_{mode}_adhoc.md`\n- Placeholders replaced: `{{FEATURE_NAME}}`, `{{FEATURE_DIR}}`, `{{PLAN_DIR}}`, `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`\n- Created in feature directory for plan mode (co-located with specs), job directory for build mode\n\n**loop.sh / loop.ps1** (`ralph_service.py:113-130`)\n- Generated script that orchestrates the iterative loop\n- Uses `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` from `portable.ralph` module\n- Platform-specific: `.ps1` on Windows, `.sh` on Unix\n- Deleted at start of each run via `_clear_runtime_artifacts()` at line 709\n\n**output.log** (`ralph_service.py:132-133`)\n- Captures stdout/stderr from the loop subprocess\n- Written in real-time as subprocess executes\n- Parsed by provider-specific parsers (`parse_stream_json_activity` for Claude, `parse_plaintext_activity` for others)\n\n**progress.txt**\n- Written by the loop script during execution (not by Python code)\n- Contains iteration markers and progress summaries\n- Read by `_read_progress()` at `ralph_service.py:656-672`\n- Format: Free-form text with markers like `ITERATION 1 complete`\n\n**IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md**\n- Written by the planning agent during plan mode\n- Location controlled by `_resolve_plan_dir()` at `ralph_service.py:591-626`:\n  1. Feature directory (`.vista/features/{slug}/`) if it exists - plans live with specs\n  2. For build mode: most recent ralph job dir with matching slug\n  3. Fallback: current job directory\n\n#### Example Job Directory Contents\n\nFrom `.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/`:\n- `job.json` - Metadata (status: completed, 2 iterations, PID 41544)\n- `task.md` - \"Spec additions were made to the diagram_representation features...\"\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - 1125-line plan with 6 phases\n- `PROMPT_plan.md` - Planning prompt with feature context\n- `progress.txt` - Iteration summaries (2 iterations logged)\n- `output.log` - (not listed in glob results, excluded from artifacts)\n\nFrom `.vista/ralph/share-docs-build/`:\n- `job.json` - Metadata (status: failed, error: \"Process ended unexpectedly\")\n- `task.md` - Build task description\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - Completed 6-step plan\n- `progress.txt` - Empty (build failed early)\n\n### Job Status Tracking Implementation\n\n#### Status Determination Logic (`ralph_service.py:324-399`)\n\n**Status Query Flow:**\n1. `get_job_status()` loads `job.json` from disk\n2. If already marked \"stopped\", returns immediately (line 333-334)\n3. Parses `output.log` for activity using provider-specific parser (line 341-343)\n4. Reads `progress.txt` for iteration markers (line 345-349)\n5. Updates `current_iteration` field from either source (line 350-351)\n6. Adds `progress_tail` array to job dict (line 352)\n\n**Process Liveness Check (`ralph_service.py:355-395`):**\n- For running jobs with PID, checks if process still alive via `_is_process_running()` at line 725\n- Validates PID belongs to this job via `_is_expected_job_process()` at line 760 (prevents stale PID reuse)\n- If process died:\n  - Checks for success via `_completed_successfully()` at line 364\n  - Success requires loop completion markers AND model activity evidence (`_has_model_activity()` at line 419)\n  - Failure shows error: \"Process ended unexpectedly (PID not alive)\" with last output tail\n\n**Platform-Specific Process Checking:**\n\nWindows (`ralph_service.py:728-753`):\n- Uses `ctypes.windll.kernel32.OpenProcess()` to get process handle\n- Checks exit code via `GetExitCodeProcess()`\n- Process is alive if exit code == STILL_ACTIVE (259)\n\nUnix (`ralph_service.py:754-758`):\n- Uses `os.kill(pid, 0)` (signal 0 doesn't kill, just checks existence)\n- Returns True if no OSError raised\n\n**Process Ownership Validation (`ralph_service.py:760-824`):**\n\nWindows validation (line 763-808):\n- Runs PowerShell `Get-CimInstance Win32_Process` to get command line\n- Checks if command line contains `loop.ps1` with matching job_dir path\n- Falls back to checking parent PID or \"python\"/\"sleep\" in command\n\nUnix validation (line 810-820):\n- Reads `/proc/{pid}/cmdline` for process arguments\n- Checks if command contains `loop.sh` with matching job_dir path\n\n### Job Lifecycle Management\n\n#### Job Creation Paths\n\n**Native Jobs (`ralph_service.py:74-176`):**\n1. Generate UUID for job_id (line 85)\n2. Create job directory at `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` or `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}` if collision (line 86-87)\n3. Clear runtime artifacts from previous runs (line 89)\n4. Resolve plan directory for feature-colocated plans (line 95)\n5. Write `task.md` (line 98-99)\n6. Generate and write `PROMPT_{mode}.md` from template (line 101-111)\n7. Generate and write platform-specific loop script (line 113-130)\n8. Open `output.log` for writing (line 132-133)\n9. Start subprocess with Popen (line 135-154)\n10. Save initial `job.json` with status \"running\" (line 157-176)\n\n**Sandboxed Jobs (`ralph_service.py:178-322`):**\n1. Check Docker availability via `ContainerManager.check_docker_available()` (line 196-202)\n2. Ensure Docker image exists via `ensure_image()` (line 205-212)\n3. Create job directory and files (steps 1-7 same as native)\n4. Generate bash loop script for container (line 236-257) - always bash, even on Windows\n5. Resolve credential mounts from settings (line 260-263)\n6. Build mount list: project RW + credentials RO (line 268-282)\n7. Create and start Docker container (line 285-293)\n8. Execute loop script inside container via `exec_in_container()` (line 296-300)\n9. Save `job.json` with `sandbox: true`, `pid: null`, `container_id: \"...\"` (line 303-322)\n\n#### Job Directory Resolution (`ralph_service.py:548-555`)\n\n**Slug-Based Directory Naming:**\n```python\nsafe_slug = \"\".join(ch for ch in slug if ch.isalnum() or ch in {\"-\", \"_\"})\nbase_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\" / safe_slug\nif not base_dir.exists():\n    return base_dir  # First job with this slug\nreturn project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\" / f\"{safe_slug}-{job_id}\"  # Collision, add UUID\n```\n\nExample: Feature \"share-docs\" in plan mode creates:\n- 1st run: `.vista/ralph/share-docs-plan/`\n- 2nd run: `.vista/ralph/share-docs-plan-{uuid}/`\n\n#### Feature-Plan Directory Co-location (`ralph_service.py:591-626`)\n\n**Plan Directory Resolution Strategy:**\n\nFor **plan mode** jobs:\n1. If `.vista/features/{slug}/` exists → plans written there (line 607-609)\n2. Otherwise → plans written to job directory\n\nFor **build mode** jobs:\n1. If `.vista/features/{slug}/` exists → read plan from there (line 607-609)\n2. Otherwise → search ralph directories for most recent `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` matching slug (line 611-624)\n3. Fallback → use job directory\n\n**Implementation:**\n```python\ndef _resolve_plan_dir(mode: str, slug: str, job_dir: Path, project_root: Path) -> Path:\n    feature_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"features\" / slug\n    if feature_dir.is_dir():\n        return feature_dir  # Plans live with specs\n    \n    if mode == \"build\":\n        # Search for most recent plan in ralph job dirs\n        ralph_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\"\n        candidates = []\n        for d in ralph_dir.iterdir():\n            if d.name.startswith(slug):\n                plan_file = d / \"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\"\n                if plan_file.exists():\n                    candidates.append((plan_file.stat().st_mtime, d))\n        if candidates:\n            candidates.sort(reverse=True)  # Most recent first\n            return candidates[0][1]\n    \n    return job_dir  # Fallback\n```\n\nThis ensures multiple plan runs update the same `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` instead of creating duplicates.\n\n### Job Discovery and Listing\n\n#### Cross-Project Job Search (`ralph.py:16-38`)\n\n**Helper Function `_find_job_context(job_id)`:**\n1. Iterates all registered projects via `ProjectService.get_all()` (line 21)\n2. For each project, checks `.vista/ralph/` directory (line 22-25)\n3. Iterates all subdirectories as potential job dirs (line 26-28)\n4. Reads `job.json` from each (line 29-36)\n5. Matches `job_id` field against search target (line 34)\n6. Returns `(project, project_root, job_dir)` tuple (line 35)\n7. Raises 404 if not found (line 38)\n\n**Used By:**\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` (line 59)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` (line 71)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` (line 98)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` (line 109)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` (line 131)\n- `POST /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/stop` (line 148)\n\n#### Job Listing (`ralph_service.py:534-546`)\n\n**Method: `list_jobs(project_root)`**\n1. Gets ralph directory at `{project_root}/.vista/ralph/` (line 536)\n2. Returns empty list if directory doesn't exist (line 537-538)\n3. Iterates all subdirectories (line 539-541)\n4. Loads `job.json` from each via `_load_job_json()` at line 578\n5. Collects jobs into list (line 542-544)\n6. Sorts by `created_at` descending (most recent first) (line 545)\n\n**API Endpoint Enhancement (`ralph.py:41-53`):**\n- Calls `ralph_service.list_jobs()` for each project\n- Enriches each job with `project_name` and `project_id` (line 49-50)\n- Merges results from all projects (line 51)\n- Re-sorts combined list by `created_at` (line 52)\n\n### Progress and Output Parsing\n\n#### Activity Extraction (`ralph_service.py:674-695`)\n\n**Method: `_read_activity(job_dir, provider)`**\n\nProvider-specific parsing dispatch:\n- **Claude provider** (line 690): Uses `parse_stream_json_activity()` from `server.services.output_parser`\n  - Expects stream-json format: `{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"text\":\"...\"}` NDJSON lines\n  - Extracts assistant messages and tool uses\n  - Returns iteration markers\n- **Other providers** (line 692): Uses `parse_plaintext_activity()`\n  - Parses human-readable tool call markers like `> Tool: Read filename.py`\n  - Extracts assistant text between tool calls\n  - Returns iteration markers\n\n**Performance Optimization:**\n- Only parses last 500 lines of output.log (line 691-692)\n- Returns last 50 activity entries as tail (line 695)\n\n**Output Format:**\n```python\n(activity_lines, iteration_number)\n# activity_lines: [\"> Tool: Read file.py\", \"Now analyzing...\", \"ITERATION 2 complete\"]\n# iteration_number: 2 (or None)\n```\n\n#### Progress File Reading (`ralph_service.py:656-672`)\n\n**Method: `_read_progress(job_dir)`**\n\nReads `progress.txt` for:\n- Last 5 lines as tail (line 661)\n- Most recent iteration number by scanning backwards for \"ITERATION\" keyword (line 663-671)\n\nReturns: `(tail_lines, iteration_number)`\n\n### Artifact Management\n\n#### Artifact Listing (`ralph.py:106-125`)\n\n**Endpoint: `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts`**\n\nFile inclusion logic:\n1. Exclude internal files: `job.json`, `output.log` (line 111)\n2. Include all other files in job directory (line 113-118)\n3. Include archived job files matching `job.*.json` pattern (line 120-124)\n\nReturns:\n```json\n{\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\"name\": \"task.md\", \"size\": 512},\n    {\"name\": \"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\", \"size\": 45678},\n    {\"name\": \"PROMPT_plan.md\", \"size\": 2048},\n    {\"name\": \"progress.txt\", \"size\": 1024}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Artifact Reading (`ralph.py:128-141`)\n\n**Endpoint: `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename:path}`**\n\nSecurity measures:\n1. Path traversal prevention via `resolve().relative_to()` check (line 134-137)\n2. Must be within job directory (raises 400 if not)\n3. Must exist and be a file (raises 404 if not, line 138-139)\n\nReturns: Plain text content with UTF-8 encoding and error replacement (line 140-141)\n\n### Dashboard Integration\n\n#### Job Detail Page (`ralph_job_detail.html`)\n\n**Layout Structure:**\n- Left sidebar (1/3 width): Job metadata + artifacts (line 19-109)\n- Main content (2/3 width): Progress terminal + output log (line 111-142)\n\n**Job Metadata Display (`ralph_job_detail.html:22-85`):**\n- Status badge with color coding (line 27-39)\n- Mode badge (plan=blue, build=green) (line 42-49)\n- Provider, model, iteration counter (line 51-62)\n- Created/completed timestamps (line 64-72)\n- Error message if failed (line 73-77)\n- Stop button if running (line 80-84)\n\n**Progress Polling (`ralph_job_detail.html:154-189`):**\n- Polls every 3 seconds for running jobs (line 156)\n- Fetches `/api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` (line 161)\n- Renders with syntax highlighting:\n  - ITERATION lines → `line-iteration` class\n  - Error/FAIL → `line-error` class  \n  - complete/PASS → `line-success` class\n- Auto-scrolls terminal to bottom (line 174)\n- Refreshes job status in parallel (line 177-188)\n- Reloads page when status changes from running (line 186)\n\n**Artifacts Section (`ralph_job_detail.html:87-108`):**\n- Lists files with sizes in KB (line 92-103)\n- Links to `/api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` (line 95-96)\n- Opens in new tab (line 96)\n\n#### Project Page Integration (`project.html:97-194`)\n\n**Ralph Loops Tab:**\n- Tab switching via `showProjectTab('loops')` function (line 31-33)\n- Loop control form for starting new jobs (line 136-191)\n- Feature selection dropdown (line 138-146)\n- Provider selection (multi-provider setups only) (line 149-160)\n- Mode selection (plan/build radio buttons) (line 163-173)\n- Model dropdown (line 177-178)\n- Max iterations input (line 182-184)\n\n**Tab State:**\n- Overview tab shows feature list with plan/arch links (line 38-94)\n- Loops tab hidden by default (line 97 - `class=\"hidden\"`)\n- No direct job listing on project page (jobs listed on dedicated `/ralph/jobs` page)\n\n### Relationship Between Features and Ralph Jobs\n\n#### No Direct Feature→Job Linking\n\n**Feature Records (`project_service.py:137-163`):**\n```python\n{\n  \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n  \"has_implementation_plan\": bool,\n  \"has_agents_md\": bool,\n  \"has_progress\": bool,\n  \"has_prompt_build\": bool,\n  \"has_prompt_plan\": bool,\n  \"spec_count\": int,\n  \"has_arch_manifest\": bool,\n  \"arch_diagram_count\": int\n}\n```\n\nNo `ralph_job_id` or job reference fields exist.\n\n**Job Records (`ralph_service.py:158-175`):**\n```python\n{\n  \"job_id\": str,\n  \"slug\": str,  # Feature name + mode suffix\n  \"mode\": str,\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe `slug` field contains the feature name but is not a foreign key.\n\n#### Implicit Linking via Slug and File Co-location\n\n**Plan Mode:**\n- If `.vista/features/{feature_name}/` exists:\n  - `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` written there (line 95-96 in `_create_native_job`)\n  - Plan becomes visible in feature metadata (line 154 in `scan_features_detailed`)\n  - Multiple plan jobs for same feature overwrite the same plan file\n\n**Build Mode:**\n- Reads plan from feature directory or searches ralph job dirs (line 611-624 in `_resolve_plan_dir`)\n- No backlink from completed build to triggering plan\n\n**Discovery Pattern:**\n- Features discovered by scanning `.vista/features/` (line 125-134 in `project_service.py`)\n- Jobs discovered by scanning `.vista/ralph/` (line 534-546 in `ralph_service.py`)\n- No SQL database or index linking the two\n- Connection inferred by slug prefix matching\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n**1. Job Creation:**\n```\nMCP Tool (spawn_teammate) \n  → ralph_service.create_job()\n    → _create_native_job() or _create_sandboxed_job()\n      → Write task.md, PROMPT_{mode}.md, loop script to job_dir\n      → Start subprocess/container\n      → Save job.json with status=\"running\"\n```\n\n**2. Job Monitoring:**\n```\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_job()\n    → _find_job_context() searches all projects\n      → ralph_service.get_job_status()\n        → Load job.json\n        → Parse output.log via provider-specific parser\n        → Check process liveness\n        → Update status if process died\n        → Save updated job.json\n        → Return enriched job dict\n```\n\n**3. Progress Polling:**\n```\nBrowser (3s interval) → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_progress()\n    → Read output.log (last 500 lines)\n    → Parse with stream-json or plaintext parser\n    → Return activity lines (last 50)\n```\n\n**4. Artifact Access:**\n```\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts\n  → ralph.py:list_ralph_artifacts()\n    → List files in job_dir (exclude job.json, output.log)\n    → Return name + size\n\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/task.md\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_artifact()\n    → Validate path within job_dir\n    → Read file content\n    → Return as plain text\n```\n\n### Key Patterns\n\n**1. Filesystem-Based Persistence:**\n- No database - all job state in `job.json` files\n- Each job directory is self-contained\n- Job discovery via directory scanning\n\n**2. Provider Abstraction:**\n- Different output formats (stream-json vs plaintext)\n- Parser dispatch based on `provider` field in job.json\n- Model activity detection varies by provider (line 429-461)\n\n**3. Plan-Feature Co-location:**\n- Plans prefer to live in `.vista/features/{slug}/` alongside specs\n- Multiple plan iterations update the same file\n- Fallback to job directory for features without feature directory\n\n**4. Security via Path Validation:**\n- All file reads validate paths via `resolve().relative_to()` pattern\n- Prevents `../` traversal attacks\n- Used in artifact reads (line 134-137) and arch file reads (`progress_service.py:89-92`)\n\n**5. Status Inference:**\n- No explicit status updates during execution\n- Status derived from process liveness + output markers\n- \"completed\" requires both loop markers AND model activity evidence\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Ralph Directory Location:**\n- Hardcoded: `.vista/ralph/` relative to project root\n- Set in `ralph_service.py:41` - `self._ralph_dir_name = \"ralph\"`\n\n**Runtime Artifacts Cleaned:**\n- `progress.txt`, `output.log`, `loop.ps1`, `loop.sh` (line 711-716)\n- Deleted before each job start to prevent stale data\n\n**Process Polling Intervals:**\n- Dashboard polls progress every 3 seconds (line 156 in `ralph_job_detail.html`)\n- No polling for completed/failed/stopped jobs\n\n**Output Parsing Limits:**\n- Last 500 lines of output.log parsed (line 691-692)\n- Last 50 activity entries returned (line 695)\n- Last 20 lines for error context (line 381)\n\n---\n\n## Relevant File References\n\n**Ralph Service Core:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py` - Job lifecycle management (830 lines)\n\n**Ralph API Routes:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py` - REST endpoints for job access (159 lines)\n\n**Dashboard Views:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\views\\ralph_job_detail.html` - Individual job monitoring UI (247 lines)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\views\\project.html` - Project page with Ralph Loops tab\n\n**Support Services:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\progress_service.py` - Read plans/progress from feature directories (128 lines)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py` - Feature scanning and metadata (164 lines)\n\n**Example Job Directories:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\.vista\\ralph\\diagram-repr-spec-planning\\` - Completed planning job (2 iterations)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\.vista\\ralph\\share-docs-build\\` - Failed build job"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aebf876 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 63882\ntool_uses: 32\nduration_ms: 199715</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99d2dbda-9327-4d38-9974-87ec95f217c6","uuid":"3ffe25e0-7fb7-404c-a350-7cd10bdcba28","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the structure of Ralph jobs in this project. Please:\n\n1. Look at a few .vista/ralph/ job directories to understand what artifacts they contain (job.json, task.md, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, progress.txt, specs/, etc.)\n2. Find any existing service that reads Ralph job data - look for ralph_service.py or similar in vista/server/services/\n3. Check the ralph routes in vista/server/routes/ to understand how jobs are currently accessed\n4. Look at how the project page and dashboard currently link features to Ralph jobs\n\nWorking directory: C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization","agentId":"aebf876","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a complete understanding of the Ralph job structure. Let me create the comprehensive analysis.\n\n## Analysis: Ralph Job Structure and Data Access\n\n### Overview\nRalph jobs are autonomous development loops that execute planning or build tasks. Each job creates a directory under `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` containing job metadata (job.json), execution logs (output.log, progress.txt), task description (task.md), prompts (PROMPT_{mode}.md), and implementation plans (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md). The system provides APIs to list, monitor, and retrieve artifacts from these jobs.\n\n### Entry Points\n\n**Job Creation:**\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:43-72` - `RalphService.create_job()` method\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:74-176` - `_create_native_job()` for local subprocess execution\n- `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py:178-322` - `_create_sandboxed_job()` for Docker container execution\n\n**Job Access APIs:**\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:41-53` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs` - List all jobs across projects\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:56-65` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` - Get single job with status\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:68-92` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` - Get parsed activity\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:95-103` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` - Get raw output log\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:106-125` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` - List artifact files\n- `vista/server/routes/ralph.py:128-141` - `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename:path}` - Read artifact content\n\n**Dashboard Views:**\n- `vista/server/views/ralph_job_detail.html:1-247` - Individual job detail page\n- `vista/server/views/ralph_jobs.html` - Job list page\n- `vista/server/views/project.html:97-194` - Ralph Loops tab in project page\n\n### Core Ralph Job Directory Structure\n\n#### Standard Files (Created by RalphService)\n\n**job.json** (`ralph_service.py:158-175` for native, `303-320` for sandboxed)\n```json\n{\n  \"job_id\": \"uuid-string\",\n  \"slug\": \"feature-name-mode\",\n  \"mode\": \"plan|build\",\n  \"status\": \"running|completed|failed|stopped\",\n  \"provider\": \"claude|opencode\",\n  \"model\": \"opus|sonnet\",\n  \"iterations\": 3,\n  \"current_iteration\": 0,\n  \"pid\": 12345,              // null for sandboxed jobs\n  \"sandbox\": false,\n  \"container_id\": null,      // Docker container ID for sandboxed jobs\n  \"created_at\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"started_at\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"completed_at\": \"ISO-8601|null\",\n  \"error\": \"error message|null\",\n  \"progress_tail\": [\"line1\", \"line2\", ...]  // Added during status queries\n}\n```\n\n**task.md** (`ralph_service.py:98-99`)\n- Created in feature directory for plan mode, job directory for build mode\n- Contains the task description passed to `create_job()`\n\n**PROMPT_{mode}.md** (`ralph_service.py:101-111`)\n- Generated from template at `vista/templates/PROMPT_{mode}_adhoc.md`\n- Placeholders replaced: `{{FEATURE_NAME}}`, `{{FEATURE_DIR}}`, `{{PLAN_DIR}}`, `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`\n- Created in feature directory for plan mode (co-located with specs), job directory for build mode\n\n**loop.sh / loop.ps1** (`ralph_service.py:113-130`)\n- Generated script that orchestrates the iterative loop\n- Uses `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` from `portable.ralph` module\n- Platform-specific: `.ps1` on Windows, `.sh` on Unix\n- Deleted at start of each run via `_clear_runtime_artifacts()` at line 709\n\n**output.log** (`ralph_service.py:132-133`)\n- Captures stdout/stderr from the loop subprocess\n- Written in real-time as subprocess executes\n- Parsed by provider-specific parsers (`parse_stream_json_activity` for Claude, `parse_plaintext_activity` for others)\n\n**progress.txt**\n- Written by the loop script during execution (not by Python code)\n- Contains iteration markers and progress summaries\n- Read by `_read_progress()` at `ralph_service.py:656-672`\n- Format: Free-form text with markers like `ITERATION 1 complete`\n\n**IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md**\n- Written by the planning agent during plan mode\n- Location controlled by `_resolve_plan_dir()` at `ralph_service.py:591-626`:\n  1. Feature directory (`.vista/features/{slug}/`) if it exists - plans live with specs\n  2. For build mode: most recent ralph job dir with matching slug\n  3. Fallback: current job directory\n\n#### Example Job Directory Contents\n\nFrom `.vista/ralph/diagram-repr-spec-planning/`:\n- `job.json` - Metadata (status: completed, 2 iterations, PID 41544)\n- `task.md` - \"Spec additions were made to the diagram_representation features...\"\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - 1125-line plan with 6 phases\n- `PROMPT_plan.md` - Planning prompt with feature context\n- `progress.txt` - Iteration summaries (2 iterations logged)\n- `output.log` - (not listed in glob results, excluded from artifacts)\n\nFrom `.vista/ralph/share-docs-build/`:\n- `job.json` - Metadata (status: failed, error: \"Process ended unexpectedly\")\n- `task.md` - Build task description\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` - Completed 6-step plan\n- `progress.txt` - Empty (build failed early)\n\n### Job Status Tracking Implementation\n\n#### Status Determination Logic (`ralph_service.py:324-399`)\n\n**Status Query Flow:**\n1. `get_job_status()` loads `job.json` from disk\n2. If already marked \"stopped\", returns immediately (line 333-334)\n3. Parses `output.log` for activity using provider-specific parser (line 341-343)\n4. Reads `progress.txt` for iteration markers (line 345-349)\n5. Updates `current_iteration` field from either source (line 350-351)\n6. Adds `progress_tail` array to job dict (line 352)\n\n**Process Liveness Check (`ralph_service.py:355-395`):**\n- For running jobs with PID, checks if process still alive via `_is_process_running()` at line 725\n- Validates PID belongs to this job via `_is_expected_job_process()` at line 760 (prevents stale PID reuse)\n- If process died:\n  - Checks for success via `_completed_successfully()` at line 364\n  - Success requires loop completion markers AND model activity evidence (`_has_model_activity()` at line 419)\n  - Failure shows error: \"Process ended unexpectedly (PID not alive)\" with last output tail\n\n**Platform-Specific Process Checking:**\n\nWindows (`ralph_service.py:728-753`):\n- Uses `ctypes.windll.kernel32.OpenProcess()` to get process handle\n- Checks exit code via `GetExitCodeProcess()`\n- Process is alive if exit code == STILL_ACTIVE (259)\n\nUnix (`ralph_service.py:754-758`):\n- Uses `os.kill(pid, 0)` (signal 0 doesn't kill, just checks existence)\n- Returns True if no OSError raised\n\n**Process Ownership Validation (`ralph_service.py:760-824`):**\n\nWindows validation (line 763-808):\n- Runs PowerShell `Get-CimInstance Win32_Process` to get command line\n- Checks if command line contains `loop.ps1` with matching job_dir path\n- Falls back to checking parent PID or \"python\"/\"sleep\" in command\n\nUnix validation (line 810-820):\n- Reads `/proc/{pid}/cmdline` for process arguments\n- Checks if command contains `loop.sh` with matching job_dir path\n\n### Job Lifecycle Management\n\n#### Job Creation Paths\n\n**Native Jobs (`ralph_service.py:74-176`):**\n1. Generate UUID for job_id (line 85)\n2. Create job directory at `.vista/ralph/{slug}/` or `.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id}` if collision (line 86-87)\n3. Clear runtime artifacts from previous runs (line 89)\n4. Resolve plan directory for feature-colocated plans (line 95)\n5. Write `task.md` (line 98-99)\n6. Generate and write `PROMPT_{mode}.md` from template (line 101-111)\n7. Generate and write platform-specific loop script (line 113-130)\n8. Open `output.log` for writing (line 132-133)\n9. Start subprocess with Popen (line 135-154)\n10. Save initial `job.json` with status \"running\" (line 157-176)\n\n**Sandboxed Jobs (`ralph_service.py:178-322`):**\n1. Check Docker availability via `ContainerManager.check_docker_available()` (line 196-202)\n2. Ensure Docker image exists via `ensure_image()` (line 205-212)\n3. Create job directory and files (steps 1-7 same as native)\n4. Generate bash loop script for container (line 236-257) - always bash, even on Windows\n5. Resolve credential mounts from settings (line 260-263)\n6. Build mount list: project RW + credentials RO (line 268-282)\n7. Create and start Docker container (line 285-293)\n8. Execute loop script inside container via `exec_in_container()` (line 296-300)\n9. Save `job.json` with `sandbox: true`, `pid: null`, `container_id: \"...\"` (line 303-322)\n\n#### Job Directory Resolution (`ralph_service.py:548-555`)\n\n**Slug-Based Directory Naming:**\n```python\nsafe_slug = \"\".join(ch for ch in slug if ch.isalnum() or ch in {\"-\", \"_\"})\nbase_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\" / safe_slug\nif not base_dir.exists():\n    return base_dir  # First job with this slug\nreturn project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\" / f\"{safe_slug}-{job_id}\"  # Collision, add UUID\n```\n\nExample: Feature \"share-docs\" in plan mode creates:\n- 1st run: `.vista/ralph/share-docs-plan/`\n- 2nd run: `.vista/ralph/share-docs-plan-{uuid}/`\n\n#### Feature-Plan Directory Co-location (`ralph_service.py:591-626`)\n\n**Plan Directory Resolution Strategy:**\n\nFor **plan mode** jobs:\n1. If `.vista/features/{slug}/` exists → plans written there (line 607-609)\n2. Otherwise → plans written to job directory\n\nFor **build mode** jobs:\n1. If `.vista/features/{slug}/` exists → read plan from there (line 607-609)\n2. Otherwise → search ralph directories for most recent `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` matching slug (line 611-624)\n3. Fallback → use job directory\n\n**Implementation:**\n```python\ndef _resolve_plan_dir(mode: str, slug: str, job_dir: Path, project_root: Path) -> Path:\n    feature_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"features\" / slug\n    if feature_dir.is_dir():\n        return feature_dir  # Plans live with specs\n    \n    if mode == \"build\":\n        # Search for most recent plan in ralph job dirs\n        ralph_dir = project_root / \".vista\" / \"ralph\"\n        candidates = []\n        for d in ralph_dir.iterdir():\n            if d.name.startswith(slug):\n                plan_file = d / \"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\"\n                if plan_file.exists():\n                    candidates.append((plan_file.stat().st_mtime, d))\n        if candidates:\n            candidates.sort(reverse=True)  # Most recent first\n            return candidates[0][1]\n    \n    return job_dir  # Fallback\n```\n\nThis ensures multiple plan runs update the same `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` instead of creating duplicates.\n\n### Job Discovery and Listing\n\n#### Cross-Project Job Search (`ralph.py:16-38`)\n\n**Helper Function `_find_job_context(job_id)`:**\n1. Iterates all registered projects via `ProjectService.get_all()` (line 21)\n2. For each project, checks `.vista/ralph/` directory (line 22-25)\n3. Iterates all subdirectories as potential job dirs (line 26-28)\n4. Reads `job.json` from each (line 29-36)\n5. Matches `job_id` field against search target (line 34)\n6. Returns `(project, project_root, job_dir)` tuple (line 35)\n7. Raises 404 if not found (line 38)\n\n**Used By:**\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}` (line 59)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` (line 71)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/output` (line 98)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts` (line 109)\n- `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` (line 131)\n- `POST /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/stop` (line 148)\n\n#### Job Listing (`ralph_service.py:534-546`)\n\n**Method: `list_jobs(project_root)`**\n1. Gets ralph directory at `{project_root}/.vista/ralph/` (line 536)\n2. Returns empty list if directory doesn't exist (line 537-538)\n3. Iterates all subdirectories (line 539-541)\n4. Loads `job.json` from each via `_load_job_json()` at line 578\n5. Collects jobs into list (line 542-544)\n6. Sorts by `created_at` descending (most recent first) (line 545)\n\n**API Endpoint Enhancement (`ralph.py:41-53`):**\n- Calls `ralph_service.list_jobs()` for each project\n- Enriches each job with `project_name` and `project_id` (line 49-50)\n- Merges results from all projects (line 51)\n- Re-sorts combined list by `created_at` (line 52)\n\n### Progress and Output Parsing\n\n#### Activity Extraction (`ralph_service.py:674-695`)\n\n**Method: `_read_activity(job_dir, provider)`**\n\nProvider-specific parsing dispatch:\n- **Claude provider** (line 690): Uses `parse_stream_json_activity()` from `server.services.output_parser`\n  - Expects stream-json format: `{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"text\":\"...\"}` NDJSON lines\n  - Extracts assistant messages and tool uses\n  - Returns iteration markers\n- **Other providers** (line 692): Uses `parse_plaintext_activity()`\n  - Parses human-readable tool call markers like `> Tool: Read filename.py`\n  - Extracts assistant text between tool calls\n  - Returns iteration markers\n\n**Performance Optimization:**\n- Only parses last 500 lines of output.log (line 691-692)\n- Returns last 50 activity entries as tail (line 695)\n\n**Output Format:**\n```python\n(activity_lines, iteration_number)\n# activity_lines: [\"> Tool: Read file.py\", \"Now analyzing...\", \"ITERATION 2 complete\"]\n# iteration_number: 2 (or None)\n```\n\n#### Progress File Reading (`ralph_service.py:656-672`)\n\n**Method: `_read_progress(job_dir)`**\n\nReads `progress.txt` for:\n- Last 5 lines as tail (line 661)\n- Most recent iteration number by scanning backwards for \"ITERATION\" keyword (line 663-671)\n\nReturns: `(tail_lines, iteration_number)`\n\n### Artifact Management\n\n#### Artifact Listing (`ralph.py:106-125`)\n\n**Endpoint: `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts`**\n\nFile inclusion logic:\n1. Exclude internal files: `job.json`, `output.log` (line 111)\n2. Include all other files in job directory (line 113-118)\n3. Include archived job files matching `job.*.json` pattern (line 120-124)\n\nReturns:\n```json\n{\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\"name\": \"task.md\", \"size\": 512},\n    {\"name\": \"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\", \"size\": 45678},\n    {\"name\": \"PROMPT_plan.md\", \"size\": 2048},\n    {\"name\": \"progress.txt\", \"size\": 1024}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### Artifact Reading (`ralph.py:128-141`)\n\n**Endpoint: `GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename:path}`**\n\nSecurity measures:\n1. Path traversal prevention via `resolve().relative_to()` check (line 134-137)\n2. Must be within job directory (raises 400 if not)\n3. Must exist and be a file (raises 404 if not, line 138-139)\n\nReturns: Plain text content with UTF-8 encoding and error replacement (line 140-141)\n\n### Dashboard Integration\n\n#### Job Detail Page (`ralph_job_detail.html`)\n\n**Layout Structure:**\n- Left sidebar (1/3 width): Job metadata + artifacts (line 19-109)\n- Main content (2/3 width): Progress terminal + output log (line 111-142)\n\n**Job Metadata Display (`ralph_job_detail.html:22-85`):**\n- Status badge with color coding (line 27-39)\n- Mode badge (plan=blue, build=green) (line 42-49)\n- Provider, model, iteration counter (line 51-62)\n- Created/completed timestamps (line 64-72)\n- Error message if failed (line 73-77)\n- Stop button if running (line 80-84)\n\n**Progress Polling (`ralph_job_detail.html:154-189`):**\n- Polls every 3 seconds for running jobs (line 156)\n- Fetches `/api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress` (line 161)\n- Renders with syntax highlighting:\n  - ITERATION lines → `line-iteration` class\n  - Error/FAIL → `line-error` class  \n  - complete/PASS → `line-success` class\n- Auto-scrolls terminal to bottom (line 174)\n- Refreshes job status in parallel (line 177-188)\n- Reloads page when status changes from running (line 186)\n\n**Artifacts Section (`ralph_job_detail.html:87-108`):**\n- Lists files with sizes in KB (line 92-103)\n- Links to `/api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/{filename}` (line 95-96)\n- Opens in new tab (line 96)\n\n#### Project Page Integration (`project.html:97-194`)\n\n**Ralph Loops Tab:**\n- Tab switching via `showProjectTab('loops')` function (line 31-33)\n- Loop control form for starting new jobs (line 136-191)\n- Feature selection dropdown (line 138-146)\n- Provider selection (multi-provider setups only) (line 149-160)\n- Mode selection (plan/build radio buttons) (line 163-173)\n- Model dropdown (line 177-178)\n- Max iterations input (line 182-184)\n\n**Tab State:**\n- Overview tab shows feature list with plan/arch links (line 38-94)\n- Loops tab hidden by default (line 97 - `class=\"hidden\"`)\n- No direct job listing on project page (jobs listed on dedicated `/ralph/jobs` page)\n\n### Relationship Between Features and Ralph Jobs\n\n#### No Direct Feature→Job Linking\n\n**Feature Records (`project_service.py:137-163`):**\n```python\n{\n  \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n  \"has_implementation_plan\": bool,\n  \"has_agents_md\": bool,\n  \"has_progress\": bool,\n  \"has_prompt_build\": bool,\n  \"has_prompt_plan\": bool,\n  \"spec_count\": int,\n  \"has_arch_manifest\": bool,\n  \"arch_diagram_count\": int\n}\n```\n\nNo `ralph_job_id` or job reference fields exist.\n\n**Job Records (`ralph_service.py:158-175`):**\n```python\n{\n  \"job_id\": str,\n  \"slug\": str,  # Feature name + mode suffix\n  \"mode\": str,\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nThe `slug` field contains the feature name but is not a foreign key.\n\n#### Implicit Linking via Slug and File Co-location\n\n**Plan Mode:**\n- If `.vista/features/{feature_name}/` exists:\n  - `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` written there (line 95-96 in `_create_native_job`)\n  - Plan becomes visible in feature metadata (line 154 in `scan_features_detailed`)\n  - Multiple plan jobs for same feature overwrite the same plan file\n\n**Build Mode:**\n- Reads plan from feature directory or searches ralph job dirs (line 611-624 in `_resolve_plan_dir`)\n- No backlink from completed build to triggering plan\n\n**Discovery Pattern:**\n- Features discovered by scanning `.vista/features/` (line 125-134 in `project_service.py`)\n- Jobs discovered by scanning `.vista/ralph/` (line 534-546 in `ralph_service.py`)\n- No SQL database or index linking the two\n- Connection inferred by slug prefix matching\n\n### Data Flow Summary\n\n**1. Job Creation:**\n```\nMCP Tool (spawn_teammate) \n  → ralph_service.create_job()\n    → _create_native_job() or _create_sandboxed_job()\n      → Write task.md, PROMPT_{mode}.md, loop script to job_dir\n      → Start subprocess/container\n      → Save job.json with status=\"running\"\n```\n\n**2. Job Monitoring:**\n```\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_job()\n    → _find_job_context() searches all projects\n      → ralph_service.get_job_status()\n        → Load job.json\n        → Parse output.log via provider-specific parser\n        → Check process liveness\n        → Update status if process died\n        → Save updated job.json\n        → Return enriched job dict\n```\n\n**3. Progress Polling:**\n```\nBrowser (3s interval) → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/progress\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_progress()\n    → Read output.log (last 500 lines)\n    → Parse with stream-json or plaintext parser\n    → Return activity lines (last 50)\n```\n\n**4. Artifact Access:**\n```\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts\n  → ralph.py:list_ralph_artifacts()\n    → List files in job_dir (exclude job.json, output.log)\n    → Return name + size\n\nBrowser → GET /api/ralph/jobs/{job_id}/artifacts/task.md\n  → ralph.py:get_ralph_artifact()\n    → Validate path within job_dir\n    → Read file content\n    → Return as plain text\n```\n\n### Key Patterns\n\n**1. Filesystem-Based Persistence:**\n- No database - all job state in `job.json` files\n- Each job directory is self-contained\n- Job discovery via directory scanning\n\n**2. Provider Abstraction:**\n- Different output formats (stream-json vs plaintext)\n- Parser dispatch based on `provider` field in job.json\n- Model activity detection varies by provider (line 429-461)\n\n**3. Plan-Feature Co-location:**\n- Plans prefer to live in `.vista/features/{slug}/` alongside specs\n- Multiple plan iterations update the same file\n- Fallback to job directory for features without feature directory\n\n**4. Security via Path Validation:**\n- All file reads validate paths via `resolve().relative_to()` pattern\n- Prevents `../` traversal attacks\n- Used in artifact reads (line 134-137) and arch file reads (`progress_service.py:89-92`)\n\n**5. Status Inference:**\n- No explicit status updates during execution\n- Status derived from process liveness + output markers\n- \"completed\" requires both loop markers AND model activity evidence\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Ralph Directory Location:**\n- Hardcoded: `.vista/ralph/` relative to project root\n- Set in `ralph_service.py:41` - `self._ralph_dir_name = \"ralph\"`\n\n**Runtime Artifacts Cleaned:**\n- `progress.txt`, `output.log`, `loop.ps1`, `loop.sh` (line 711-716)\n- Deleted before each job start to prevent stale data\n\n**Process Polling Intervals:**\n- Dashboard polls progress every 3 seconds (line 156 in `ralph_job_detail.html`)\n- No polling for completed/failed/stopped jobs\n\n**Output Parsing Limits:**\n- Last 500 lines of output.log parsed (line 691-692)\n- Last 50 activity entries returned (line 695)\n- Last 20 lines for error context (line 381)\n\n---\n\n## Relevant File References\n\n**Ralph Service Core:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\ralph_service.py` - Job lifecycle management (830 lines)\n\n**Ralph API Routes:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\routes\\ralph.py` - REST endpoints for job access (159 lines)\n\n**Dashboard Views:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\views\\ralph_job_detail.html` - Individual job monitoring UI (247 lines)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\views\\project.html` - Project page with Ralph Loops tab\n\n**Support Services:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\progress_service.py` - Read plans/progress from feature directories (128 lines)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\vista\\server\\services\\project_service.py` - Feature scanning and metadata (164 lines)\n\n**Example Job Directories:**\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\.vista\\ralph\\diagram-repr-spec-planning\\` - Completed planning job (2 iterations)\n- `C:\\Users\\Grove\\OneDrive\\Documents\\PYTHON\\claude_plugins\\vista-expanded-visualization\\.vista\\ralph\\share-docs-build\\` - Failed build job"}],"totalDurationMs":199715,"totalTokens":63882,"totalToolUseCount":32,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":55892,"output_tokens":6755,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
